tion/problem "$4\\operatorname{sin}⁡({70}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({70}^{∘})\\operatorname{csc}⁡({140}^{∘})=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={70}^{∘}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({70}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({70}^{∘}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot {70}^{∘})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡({140}^{∘})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\operatorname{sin}⁡({70}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({70}^{∘})\\operatorname{csc}⁡({140}^{∘}) & =2\\cdot [2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({70}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({70}^{∘})]\\operatorname{csc}⁡({140}^{∘}) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({140}^{∘})\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡({140}^{∘})} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-120088/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d820aa9f-7c02-53b5-9b09-c25ee59dbdaf"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-120088"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-120093/selection/ba4f93c665eeb1d3119190b9d55cefe3cc9a2e4ac6c6f214e083029332e7ade6" :answer/id #uuid "0ab05e73-82ad-52f4-a357-d39564af9b29" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120093/selection/762be4f572111746c3aa78ff27df20fd279fd33dd046189e788f42b03dd4b4f6" :answer/id #uuid "7e61e5ed-c231-5185-8815-d44b78296c3e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120093/selection/c529c3d7f2228e2af401508f8697bdf6904adc18869204beaa37ff5c66a46310" :answer/id #uuid "eafad791-a5a2-5418-b303-498574d1f026" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120093/selection/61833d3dbb4fef54327042746daa8ead0386bd2a92f1aa1e3b231d08c61f604d" :answer/id #uuid "a59e81c7-2352-5725-8019-694ce6dfe647" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120093/selection/46007f6415e3526b4dcecd86f71e430a26e289b37399831444d48bff3d6e66ec" :answer/id #uuid "ca4d5e4a-9f18-51b3-8f74-7eeda4b99e9d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120093/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "56867213-51d1-5383-88a5-d1358794594a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-120093/selection/61833d3dbb4fef54327042746daa8ead0386bd2a92f1aa1e3b231d08c61f604d" :answer-field/choices ["q-120093/selection/ba4f93c665eeb1d3119190b9d55cefe3cc9a2e4ac6c6f214e083029332e7ade6" "q-120093/selection/762be4f572111746c3aa78ff27df20fd279fd33dd046189e788f42b03dd4b4f6" "q-120093/selection/c529c3d7f2228e2af401508f8697bdf6904adc18869204beaa37ff5c66a46310" "q-120093/selection/61833d3dbb4fef54327042746daa8ead0386bd2a92f1aa1e3b231d08c61f604d" "q-120093/selection/46007f6415e3526b4dcecd86f71e430a26e289b37399831444d48bff3d6e66ec"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-120093" :question/id #uuid "9f316510-778b-5c23-bcf2-6b309d414374" :question/math-academy-id "q-120093" :question/problem "$8\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{32})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{32})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{32}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{32})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{32})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{32})\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies as\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{32})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{32})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16}).\n$$\n\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{32})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{32})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16}) & =4[2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{32})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{32})]\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16}) \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the double-angle formula once more with $x=\\frac{\\pi }{16},$ we can further simplify the above expression: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16}) & =2[2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})] \\\\  & =2[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{16})] \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-120093/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d820aa9f-7c02-53b5-9b09-c25ee59dbdaf"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-120093"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
